      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسْمِعٌ</span></b>  [act. part. n. of 4, q. v.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسْمِعَةٌ</span> <i>A female singer.</i> (S, K.) [See an ex. of
the pl. in a verse cited voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَارِبٌ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And
hence, (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زمر</span>,) the former is applied to
(tropical:)  <i>A shackle.</i> (K, and TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زمر</span>.)

